Observers noted the change could affect aerodynamic loads and tower interface geometry. The image originates from an FAA filing and an accompanying ex-post. The updated proportions reflect ongoing iteration on the upper stage tank design ahead of future flight tests. The next static fire tests will validate revised stack frequencies and control bandwidth. The US Space Force is extending star shield connectivity to additional military aircraft platforms.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:15.820
The move builds on existing star shield contracts that already supply secure broadband to government users. No specific aircraft types or contract values were disclosed in the announcement. The expansion keeps star shield on a separate hardware and spectrum path from the commercial starlink constellation.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:38.140
Star Shield continues to serve national security missions distinct from the commercial constellations direct to cell and residential offerings. XAI closed a new funding round that adds several billion dollars to its balance sheet. The capital will support continued scaling of the Colossus class training clusters. No valuation or lead investor details were released.

