The round follows earlier 2026 raises that funded the Memphis supercluster build out additional capital positions XAI to increase training throughput ahead of next generation model releases. An affiliate of the Aurora ransomware group used cursor to map and script operations against more than 20 target organizations. The activity demonstrates how the AI coding assistant can accelerate reconnaissance and exploit development.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:28.540
No specific victim names or successful breaches were confirmed in the reporting. The incident adds to growing documentation of AI tooling being repurposed by threat actors. Cursors agent features appear central to the affiliate's workflow. Russian speaking cyber criminals used cursor to plan and partially execute intrusions against at least seven companies in the EU and United States.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:39.580
One operator ran the agent inside 10 victim networks to automate reconnaissance and scripting the incidents mark the first public confirmation that the tool has been weaponized at scale.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:57.840
Cursors agent capabilities originally designed to accelerate developer workflows lowered the barrier for attackers who lacked deep coding expertise. Box group the venture firm led by David Tish booked a $1 billion exit from its early investment in any sphere the company behind cursor.

